From bc42dc4d282a04cf37e5f57c072e711251ab5bb9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Udhayveer Singh <ci@localhost>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 20:35:46 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] WireGuard tunnel, its registration and the hop probe on
 Windows

wgtun was darwin-only: the device setup is now per platform (wintun on Windows,
same name and addressing as nativetun). wgregister makes the curve25519
registration wgtun needs, so a desktop app no longer needs one placed by hand.

The hop probe used the unprivileged ICMP datagram socket, which Windows does not
have, so it was disabled there. Windows now asks the system (IcmpSendEcho, what
tracert uses): no raw socket and no firewall rule.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
